Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin announced Wednesday on X: “We are DELIGHTED to announce that Kilmar Abrego Garcia has self-deported from the United States to Spain.” He added: “We promised the American people that this human trafficker, wife beater, gang member, and child predator would not remain in our country. This Salvadoran man will no longer terrorize innocent Americans.”
We are DELIGHTED to announce that Kilmar Abrego Garcia has self-deported from the United States to Spain. We promised the American people that this human trafficker, wife beater, gang member, and child predator would not remain in our country. This Salvadoran man will no longer…— Secretary Markwayne Mullin (@SecMullinDHS) November 25, 2026
[NOTE: Mullin’s post cites no evidence for those labels. Abrego Garcia pleaded not guilty to the federal human-smuggling charges, and a judge dismissed that case in May. He denies being a member of MS-13. The Justice Department has appealed the dismissal.]
Sen. Chris Van Hollen (D-MD), who pressed for Abrego Garcia’s release from El Salvador’s CECOT prison, responded: “Today, Kilmar Abrego Garcia is a free man. I am grateful that he finally received the due process he, and every single person in our country, is owed.” He continued: “We can never compromise when it comes to our Constitutional rights.”
Today, Kilmar Abrego Garcia is a free man. I am grateful that he finally received the due process he, and every single person in our country, is owed.We can never compromise when it comes to our Constitutional rights. pic.twitter.com/uZJYgaHMO4— Senator Chris Van Hollen (@ChrisVanHollen) November 25, 2026
Abrego Garcia said in a statement, “I am leaving happy. I am leaving with my freedom.”
His attorney, Simon Sandoval-Moshenberg, described the move as temporary, saying his client is “waiting out the end of this administration.” The Trump administration had tried to send Abrego Garcia to Uganda, Eswatini, Ghana and, most recently, Liberia.
In June, Mullin told Van Hollen at a Senate hearing that DHS “will be happy to send” Abrego Garcia to Costa Rica if he was willing to go. DHS officials and Justice Department attorneys had been saying otherwise in court for months.
[NOTE: DHS added to the announcement: “To be clear: Kilmar Abrego Garcia departed the United States pursuant to a removal order. He paid for his own flight and received no incentives. He will NEVER be allowed back inside the United States.”]
The department also posted a photo of Trump waving his hand outside of a take-out McDonald’s window and wrote: “It’s not surprising this criminal illegal alien would choose to go to Spain, a country that earlier this year was invaded by tens of thousands of illegal aliens. Spain’s radical open-border policies have made the once-great country a breeding ground for illegal migrants. Good riddance.”
Kilmar Abrego Garcia has self deported to Spain.
